  "markdown": "# Investigation report\n\n**Question:** Which Backblaze drive models had the highest annualized failure rate in Q2 2026 among models with at least 60 drives, and is the top one significantly worse than the fleet?\n\n**Scope:** source backblaze; from 2026-04-01; to 2026-06-30 \u00b7 **Mode:** single \u00b7 **Model:** `openai/gpt-oss-20b` \u00b7 **Status:** completed\n\n## Summary\n\n- ST10000NM0086 had the highest annualized failure rate ([9.75](evidence:ev_06629538b58916c6)%) in Q2\u202f2026 among models with at least 60 drives, about [5.6](evidence:ev_06629538b58916c6) times the fleet average and statistically significant. ([1.73777](evidence:ev_06a0c6765eb148d6), [1.07923e-10](evidence:ev_064cf74cbea0cb4f))\n\n## Findings\n\n- ST10000NM0086 had an AFR of [9.75](evidence:ev_06629538b58916c6)% in Q2\u202f2026, the highest among models with at least 60 drives.\n- ST14000NM0138 had an AFR of [8.26](evidence:ev_06629538b58916c6)%, the second\u2011highest in the same cohort.\n- The fleet AFR for Q2\u202f2026 was [1.74](evidence:ev_06a0c6765eb148d6)%.\n- The rate ratio of ST10000NM0086 versus the fleet was [5.61](evidence:ev_06629538b58916c6), with a p\u2011value of 1.08\u00d710\u207b\u00b9\u2070, indicating a statistically significant difference. ([1.07923e-10](evidence:ev_064cf74cbea0cb4f))\n- All listed models had at least 60 drives, satisfying the minimum sample size requirement. [ev_06629538b58916c6](evidence:ev_06629538b58916c6)\n\n## Hypotheses\n\n1. **A manufacturing defect in the ST10000NM0086 line caused the elevated failure rate.** (confidence: medium)\n   - ST10000NM0086 had an AFR of [9.75](evidence:ev_06629538b58916c6)%, [5.6](evidence:ev_06629538b58916c6) times the fleet average. ([1.73777](evidence:ev_06a0c6765eb148d6))\n   - _How to confirm:_ Inspect production logs and failure modes for ST10000NM0086 to identify common root causes.\n2. **The high AFR is due to a narrow usage window in Q2 2026, not a systemic defect.** (confidence: low)\n   - The fleet AFR was [1.74](evidence:ev_06a0c6765eb148d6)%, suggesting overall reliability was acceptable.\n   - _How to confirm:_ Compare usage patterns (temperature, workload) of ST10000NM0086 to other models.\n\n## Recommended actions\n\n- Review failure reports for ST10000NM0086 to identify common failure modes.\n- Cross\u2011check manufacturing lot data for ST10000NM0086 against other models.\n- Update monitoring thresholds for ST10000NM0086 drives to trigger earlier alerts.\n- Run a targeted field test on a fresh cohort of ST10000NM0086 to confirm the AFR.\n- Document any deviations in operating conditions that could explain the elevated rate.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- Small cohort: fewer than 60 drives or fewer than 3 failures make AFR unstable; read the 95% interval, not the point estimate.\n- Backblaze data: drives that fail on their first day are not captured.\n- Only models with \u226560 drives are included; smaller cohorts may have higher AFRs.\n- Confidence intervals for some models are wide (e.g., ST14000NM0018).\n- The analysis assumes the fleet AFR represents all other models collectively.\n- Data is limited to the Q2\u202f2026 period; longer\u2011term trends are unknown.\n\n## Unverified\n\n_Every claim passed the evidence check._\n"
 },
